se plugin to run FiveNet using containers.",[191,203,204,205,211],{},"Please use one of the many guides available on the internet to install Docker Engine and Docker Compose on your server, for example ",[206,207,208],"a",{"href":208,"rel":209},"https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.docker.com\u002Fengine\u002Finstall\u002F",[210],"nofollow",".",[191,213,214,215,219],{},"Depending on your server's operating system, make sure to start the Docker Daemon using ",[216,217,218],"code",{},"systemctl start docker"," .",[191,221,222],{},"To check that Docker and the Docker Compose plugin are ready, you can use the following commands:",[224,225,230],"pre",{"className":226,"code":227,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","docker version\ndocker compose version\n","bash","",[216,231,232,245],{"__ignoreMap":229},[233,234,237,241],"span",{"class":235,"line":236},"line",1,[233,238,240],{"class":239},"sBMFI","docker",[233,242,244],{"class":243},"sfazB"," version\n",[233,246,248,250,253],{"class":235,"line":247},2,[233,249,240],{"class":239},[233,251,252],{"class":243}," compose",[233,254,244],{"class":243},[191,256,257,258,261],{},"You can now continue with preparing the ",[216,259,260],{},"docker-compose.yaml"," file for your setup.",[195,263,265,266],{"id":264},"_2-prepare-docker-composeyaml","2. Prepare ",[216,267,260],{},[269,270,271],"callout",{},[191,272,273,274,211],{},"Container images are available from ",[206,275,278],{"href":276,"rel":277},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffivenet-app\u002Ffivenet\u002Fpkgs\u002Fcontainer\u002Ffivenet",[210],"GHCR.io fivenet-app\u002Ffivenet registry",[191,280,281,282,289],{},"Use the ",[206,283,286,288],{"href":284,"rel":285},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffivenet-app\u002Ffivenet\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fdocker-compose.yaml",[210],[216,287,260],{}," example file"," as a starting point.",[191,291,292],{},"Review the example file and adjust it for your environment before starting the stack. In particular, make sure to check:",[294,295,296,320,323,326],"ul",{},[297,298,299,300,305,306,310,311],"li",{},"The image tags you want to deploy (e.g., a ",[206,301,304],{"href":302,"rel":303},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffivenet-app\u002Ffivenet\u002Freleases",[210],"release"," or a ",[206,307,309],{"href":276,"rel":308},[210],"development version",").\n",[294,312,313],{},[297,314,315,316,319],{},"It is recommended to use the latest stable release tag for production deployments, you shouldn't ",[216,317,318],{},"latest"," tag.",[297,321,322],{},"Environment variables and mounted files.",[297,324,325],{},"Database, NATS, and other service connection settings.",[297,327,328],{},"Domain or reverse-proxy related settings if you expose FiveNet externally.",[191,330,331,332,335],{},"If you already have a Docker NGINX Reverse Proxy or a similar solution for exposing your container applications to the internet, you can remove or comment out the ",[216,333,334],{},"nginx-proxy"," container from the example file.\nWhen using the Docker NGINX Reverse Proxy, make sure to update the environment variables of each container so they match the domain or subdomain you want to use.",[269,337,338],{},[191,339,340,341,211],{},"To build the FiveNet container image yourself, you need to fulfill the ",[206,342,344],{"href":343},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Frequirements#development","development requirements setup",[191,346,347,348,350,351,354,355,358,359,211],{},"If you use the NATS server from the default ",[216,349,260],{},", the ",[216,352,353],{},"nats.url"," in your FiveNet ",[216,356,357],{},"config.yaml"," should look like this: ",[216,360,361],{},"url: \"nats:\u002F\u002Ffivenet:fivenet_topsecret@localhost:4222\"",[195,363,365],{"id":364},"_21-prepare-fivenet-config","2.1. Prepare FiveNet Config",[269,367,371],{"color":368,"icon":369,"to":370},"secondary","i-mdi-head-idea","https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffivenet-app\u002Ffivenet\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fconfig.example.yaml",[191,372,373],{},"Make sure to start using the example config file (click here) and modify it as you need.",[191,375,376,377,386,387,389],{},"Check the ",[206,378,380,381,385],{"href":379},"..\u002Fconfiguration\u002Fconfig-reference#must-set-config-options","configuration reference page ",[382,383,384],"strong",{},"\"Must Set Config Options\""," section and reference list"," to create a working ",[216,388,357],{}," for FiveNet.",[195,391,393],{"id":392},"_22-prepare-fivenet-dbsync-config","2.2. Prepare FiveNet DBSync Config",[269,395,397],{"color":368,"icon":369,"to":396},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffivenet-app\u002Ffivenet\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fdbsync.example.yaml",[191,398,373],{},[191,400,376,401,386,405,408],{},[206,402,404],{"href":403},"..\u002Fconfiguration\u002Fdbsync","DBSync page",[216,406,407],{},"dbsync.yaml"," for FiveNet DBSync.",[195,410,412],{"id":411},"_3-run-fivenet","3. Run FiveNet",[191,414,415],{},"Pull the latest container images and start the server, dbsync, worker, and discord bot containers:",[224,417,419],{"className":226,"code":418,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"docker compose pull\ndocker compose up -d\n",[216,420,421,430],{"__ignoreMap":229},[233,422,423,425,427],{"class":235,"line":236},[233,424,240],{"class":239},[233,426,252],{"class":243},[233,428,429],{"class":243}," pull\n",[233,431,432,434,436,439],{"class":235,"line":247},[233,433,240],{"class":239},[233,435,252],{"class":243},[233,437,438],{"class":243}," up",[233,440,441],{"class":243}," -d\n",[195,443,445],{"id":444},"_4-verify-the-deployment","4. Verify the Deployment",[191,447,448],{},"After the containers are running, verify that the stack started correctly:",[224,450,452],{"className":226,"code":451,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"docker compose ps\ndocker compose logs --tail=100\n",[216,453,454,463],{"__ignoreMap":229},[233,455,456,458,460],{"class":235,"line":236},[233,457,240],{"class":239},[233,459,252],{"class":243},[233,461,462],{"class":243}," ps\n",[233,464,465,467,469,472],{"class":235,"line":247},[233,466,240],{"class":239},[233,468,252],{"class":243},[233,470,471],{"class":243}," logs",[233,473,474],{"class":243}," --tail=100\n",[191,476,477],{},"Make sure the FiveNet containers are healthy and that the application is reachable through your configured domain, reverse proxy, or local access path.",[195,479,481],{"id":480},"_5-reverse-proxy-recommendations","5. Reverse Proxy Recommendations",[191,483,484,485,490,491,494,495,498],{},"If you are not already using a reverse proxy to expose FiveNet, consider a solution such as ",[206,486,489],{"href":487,"rel":488},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fnginx-proxy\u002Fnginx-proxy",[210],"nginx-proxy\u002Fnginx-proxy"," to safely expose the FiveNet server (",[216,492,493],{},"\u002F",") and the Iconify API container (",[216,496,497],{},"\u002Fapi\u002Ficons",").",[195,500,502],{"id":501},"_51-configuring-traefik-as-a-reverse-proxy","5.1. Configuring Traefik as a Reverse Proxy",[191,504,505],{},"If you prefer using Traefik as your reverse proxy, follow these steps to configure it for FiveNet:",[507,508,509,521,527,550,642],"ol",{},[297,510,511,514,515,520],{},[382,512,513],{},"Install Traefik",": Refer to the ",[206,516,519],{"href":517,"rel":518},"https:\u002F\u002Fdoc.traefik.io\u002Ftraefik\u002Fgetting-started\u002Finstallation\u002F",[210],"Traefik documentation"," for installation instructions.",[297,522,523,526],{},[382,524,525],{},"Start Traefik",": Run Traefik alongside your FiveNet containers using Docker Compose.",[297,528,529,532,533,538,539],{},[382,530,531],{},"HTTPS\u002FTLS Setup",": Follow the ",[206,534,537],{"href":535,"rel":536},"https:\u002F\u002Fdoc.traefik.io\u002Ftraefik\u002Fhttps\u002Ftls\u002F",[210],"Traefik HTTPS\u002FTLS setup documentation"," to configure secure connections.",[294,540,541],{},[297,542,543,544,549],{},"Ensure GRPC\u002FH2C support is enabled for the service. Refer to ",[206,545,548],{"href":546,"rel":547},"https:\u002F\u002Fdoc.traefik.io\u002Ftraefik\u002Fuser-guides\u002Fgrpc\u002F#with-http-h2c",[210],"Traefik GRPC With HTTP (h2c)"," for more guidance.",[297,551,552,555,556,559,560,562,563],{},[382,553,554],{},"Label the Containers",": Add the following labels to the ",[382,557,558],{},"FiveNet server container"," in your ",[216,561,260],{}," file:",[224,564,568],{"className":565,"code":566,"language":567,"meta":229,"style":229},"language-yaml shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","labels:\n  - \"traefik.enable=true\"\n  - \"traefik.http.routers.fivenet.rule=Host(`your-domain.com`)\"\n  - \"traefik.http.routers.fivenet.entrypoints=websecure\"\n  - \"traefik.http.routers.fivenet.tls.certresolver=myresolver\"\n  - \"traefik.http.services.fivenet.loadbalancer.server.scheme=h2c\"\n","yaml",[216,569,570,580,594,606,618,630],{"__ignoreMap":229},[233,571,572,576],{"class":235,"line":236},[233,573,575],{"class":574},"swJcz","labels",[233,577,579],{"class":578},"sMK4o",":\n",[233,581,582,585,588,591],{"class":235,"line":247},[233,583,584],{"class":578},"  -",[233,586,587],{"class":578}," \"",[233,589,590],{"class":243},"traefik.enable=true",[233,592,593],{"class":578},"\"\n",[233,595,597,599,601,604],{"class":235,"line":596},3,[233,598,584],{"class":578},[233,600,587],{"class":578},[233,602,603],{"class":243},"traefik.http.routers.fivenet.rule=Host(`your-domain.com`)",[233,605,593],{"class":578},[233,607,609,611,613,616],{"class":235,"line":608},4,[233,610,584],{"class":578},[233,612,587],{"class":578},[233,614,615],{"class":243},"traefik.http.routers.fivenet.entrypoints=websecure",[233,617,593],{"class":578},[233,619,621,623,625,628],{"class":235,"line":620},5,[233,622,584],{"class":578},[233,624,587],{"class":578},[233,626,627],{"class":243},"traefik.http.routers.fivenet.tls.certresolver=myresolver",[233,629,593],{"class":578},[233,631,633,635,637,640],{"class":235,"line":632},6,[233,634,584],{"class":578},[233,636,587],{"class":578},[233,638,639],{"class":243},"traefik.http.services.fivenet.loadbalancer.server.scheme=h2c",[233,641,593],{"class":578},[297,643,644,647],{},[382,645,646],{},"Verify Configuration",": Ensure that your domain points to the server's IP and that Traefik is correctly routing traffic to the FiveNet containers.",[191,649,650],{},"This setup allows you to securely expose FiveNet to the internet using Traefik.",[195,652,654],{"id":653},"_6-post-installation-steps","6. Post-Installation Steps",[191,656,657,658,662],{},"Make sure to follow the ",[206,659,661],{"href":660},"post-install-steps","post-installation steps"," now.",[664,665,667],"h3",{"id":666},"troubleshooting","Troubleshooting",[191,669,670,671,675],{},"If you face issues during the containerized installation, such as database collation mismatches, check the ",[206,672,674],{"href":673},"..\u002Fconfiguration\u002Fcommon-installation-issues","Common Installation Issues"," page for solutions.",[677,678,679],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default